        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Milan</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 590 BCE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">Around 590 BCE a Celtic tribe of the Insubres group, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golasecca-culture">Golasecca culture</a>, settled it as Medhelanon; in the legend reported by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy</a> it was founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bellovesus">Bellovesus</a> in the reign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarquinius-priscus">Tarquinius Priscus</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">In the north-western part of the Po Valley in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, about halfway between the river Po and the foothills of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ticino">Ticino</a> to the west and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adda">Adda</a> to the east.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">Mediolanum as an imperial seat; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edict-of-milan">Edict of Milan</a> of 313; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ambrose">Ambrose</a>; the Visconti and Sforza dukes; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leonardo-da-vinci">Leonardo da Vinci</a>’s Last Supper; the Cathedral and the Castello Sforzesco; the Five Days of 1848</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Milan is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a> and the second-largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, with about 1.36 million people in the city proper.</span></div>
